WEBVTT

00:03.160 --> 00:06.770
Fight for your justice,
show your courage.

00:06.770 --> 00:10.370
Right! Grasp truth in these hands.

00:10.370 --> 00:13.780
Fight for your justice, I want you

00:13.780 --> 00:21.200
as you fight through
with your head held up high.

00:35.860 --> 00:39.930
Rather than polishing diamonds

00:43.040 --> 00:46.970
give me a glistening future.

00:50.250 --> 00:52.480
Even if nothing's there, get up.

00:52.480 --> 00:56.350
It's important to turn on the switch.

00:57.450 --> 01:00.220
Something new that I don't want to yield.

01:00.220 --> 01:04.750
Seeking it is justice!

01:06.360 --> 01:09.930
Fight for your justice,
be serious about it.

01:09.930 --> 01:13.540
Right! Face reality head on.

01:13.540 --> 01:16.940
Fight for your justice,
I love how you

01:16.940 --> 01:27.340
never give up even if
the current is against you.

01:29.020 --> 01:31.010
"I want to change..."

01:33.490 --> 01:36.480
"I want to escape from
the bottom of the dark shadows."

01:39.130 --> 01:42.120
"That was all when
I started this journey..."
That was all when
I started this journey...

01:52.070 --> 01:55.240
It's true that many
parts have been fortified.

01:55.240 --> 01:58.450
We can get past
small magnetic storms now.

01:58.450 --> 01:59.950
Is everyone watching?

01:59.950 --> 02:05.520
The new version of Vandread
Jura will tow you over to Mejale!

02:05.520 --> 02:07.320
You all should be grateful!

02:17.770 --> 02:19.430
Soon...

02:22.170 --> 02:23.830
Soon...

02:34.120 --> 02:35.920
Was it a long journey...

02:35.920 --> 02:37.350
Or...

02:37.350 --> 02:40.810
All right,
we're gonna rush through this now!

02:45.460 --> 02:48.760
Please, even after I get back to Mejale...

02:48.760 --> 02:51.790
I hope I can still be with Mr. Alien.

03:06.780 --> 03:08.220
Just a little more.

03:08.220 --> 03:09.850
I'm glad, ribbit.

03:09.850 --> 03:11.920
This is stupid!

03:11.920 --> 03:13.250
When you get to Mejale...

03:13.250 --> 03:16.930
...you, you,
and you might all be harvested!

03:16.930 --> 03:19.390
You're so easygoing!

03:19.390 --> 03:20.700
That's so cruel!

03:20.700 --> 03:22.730
Why are you saying that?

03:22.730 --> 03:26.030
Sorry, but Mejale
has nothing to do with me.

03:26.030 --> 03:28.640
That's all. See ya!

03:28.640 --> 03:30.100
She's so snotty!

03:30.100 --> 03:32.330
Thinking it's someone else's business!

03:37.210 --> 03:38.750
Come on, what is it?

03:38.750 --> 03:41.750
Can we really get back like this?

03:41.750 --> 03:42.850
Don't you fret.

03:42.850 --> 03:45.550
This can't scare you.

03:45.550 --> 03:47.860
We'll make sure to get back there.

03:47.860 --> 03:50.290
And I'll see with my own eyes...

03:50.290 --> 03:51.990
our future.

03:54.100 --> 03:55.730
You're so mature.

03:55.730 --> 03:57.790
What happened to you as of late?

04:06.470 --> 04:08.110
Looks like the trembling's gone.

04:08.110 --> 04:10.580
That was dangerous, ribbit.

04:10.580 --> 04:13.170
Mr. Alien's really doing his best!

04:14.250 --> 04:16.050
Mr. Alien!

04:16.050 --> 04:17.020
What is it?

04:17.020 --> 04:18.350
Good work!

04:18.350 --> 04:22.220
I'll be waiting with yummy food,
so let's party when you get back!

04:22.220 --> 04:23.860
Sure!

04:23.860 --> 04:26.260
What? Just the two of you?

04:26.260 --> 04:28.230
Don't pout!

04:28.230 --> 04:30.600
I'll be making your share, Jura.

04:30.600 --> 04:32.630
So look forward to it!

04:32.630 --> 04:36.040
Barnette! You're just so kind!

04:36.040 --> 04:38.010
That's a definite, definite promise!

04:38.010 --> 04:39.740
I'll be back really soon!

04:40.840 --> 04:43.240
Geez, she's so...

04:43.240 --> 04:45.480
Hey, this may sound strange...

04:45.480 --> 04:49.580
But even if you were to be
friends with Dita, you're a guy.

04:49.580 --> 04:51.750
You can't go down to Mejale.

04:51.750 --> 04:53.220
That's not important.

04:53.220 --> 04:57.460
Fighting the harvest is more
important than stuff like that!

04:57.460 --> 04:58.560
That's right!

04:58.560 --> 05:02.030
I'll fight alongside Mr. Alien forever!

05:02.030 --> 05:04.500
Then why don't you make a baby?

05:05.530 --> 05:08.870
Quit the nonsense
and concentrate for now!

05:10.340 --> 05:12.240
Not honest, are you?

05:16.780 --> 05:19.010
Doctor, how's it going?

05:20.180 --> 05:22.680
Not bad.

05:22.680 --> 05:24.020
I just realized...

05:24.020 --> 05:27.290
When you're happy,
you tend to drop your tone of voice.

05:27.290 --> 05:29.760
That's the opposite of normal people.

05:29.760 --> 05:33.090
Should I be thankful
that you observe me?

05:35.030 --> 05:36.830
Maybe I'm nervous...

05:36.830 --> 05:38.830
My heart skipped a beat just now.

05:38.830 --> 05:40.500
Shall I examine you?

05:40.500 --> 05:42.160
I'm all right.

05:47.080 --> 05:48.380
Geez, so stupid.

05:48.380 --> 05:51.650
Everywhere I look, they're
bouncing around like little kids!

05:51.650 --> 05:54.810
Fine, I'm just an outsider, right, Q?

05:58.150 --> 05:59.810
I thought so...

06:05.130 --> 06:06.830
What's wrong with the Paksis?

06:06.830 --> 06:08.460
Extra, extra!

06:08.460 --> 06:13.870
We're celebrating our return
to Mejale and Tarak with a banquet!

06:17.140 --> 06:18.710
Why are you pouting?

06:18.710 --> 06:20.610
I'm not pouting!

06:20.610 --> 06:23.370
Are you lonely?

06:24.750 --> 06:26.450
Lonely?

06:26.450 --> 06:29.980
There's no way that
I would ever be lonely!

06:29.980 --> 06:33.280
I'm right! I'm right!

06:41.260 --> 06:42.400
Alone.

06:42.400 --> 06:44.500
- Solitude. Doubt.
- W-What?

06:44.500 --> 06:45.760
What's wrong with you?

06:48.000 --> 06:50.070
Doubt of having nowhere to return.

06:50.070 --> 06:52.370
Solitude of being a different race.

06:52.370 --> 06:53.940
What are you talking about?

06:53.940 --> 06:56.740
I'm totally fine even if I'm by myself!

06:56.740 --> 07:00.720
It's much better to be here
than being with all those kids!

07:00.720 --> 07:02.680
Could it be that the Paksis...

07:06.390 --> 07:08.390
You know...

07:08.390 --> 07:10.490
What do you think about the way

07:10.490 --> 07:13.260
men and women were
meant to have babies?

07:13.260 --> 07:15.000
W-What do I...

07:15.000 --> 07:17.570
Would you like to try it out with me?

07:17.570 --> 07:19.130
D-Don't be so foolish!

07:19.130 --> 07:22.640
I don't know how
to make one for starters!

07:22.640 --> 07:25.970
Then why did you take Ezra's baby?

07:25.970 --> 07:28.110
It's not that I wanted to.

07:28.110 --> 07:31.710
You won't be a good
ohma if you're like that.

07:31.710 --> 07:33.950
You mean a parent?

07:33.950 --> 07:38.920
I wonder what I'll give
my kids if I become a parent...

07:38.920 --> 07:40.760
You're still a kid yourself.

07:40.760 --> 07:43.720
Well, it's true that
I don't sound convincing.

07:43.720 --> 07:46.990
If I say anything,
let it be after I show results, huh?

07:48.130 --> 07:49.860
You really did change.

07:52.230 --> 07:54.630
- I'm back!
- Welcome back.

07:56.940 --> 07:59.810
What's this?

07:59.810 --> 08:02.440
They've already started the banquet!

08:06.510 --> 08:09.080
It looks pretty lively...

08:09.080 --> 08:10.520
I'm not good with crowds.

08:10.520 --> 08:13.420
Then don't stray from my side!

08:20.860 --> 08:23.960
Duero and Parfet were in
that kind of a relationship?

08:28.800 --> 08:30.790
The vice-captain is alone...

08:32.370 --> 08:35.840
Could this be the perfect opportunity?

08:35.840 --> 08:39.110
No, I can't let this
go as a social prince.

08:39.110 --> 08:41.580
I must be straightforward.

08:48.520 --> 08:50.390
You're lonely, too?

08:50.390 --> 08:52.960
Analyzing human emotions.

08:52.960 --> 08:57.200
Paksis once fused and
separated on its own will.

08:57.200 --> 09:00.770
It split during the
research of this dimension.

09:00.770 --> 09:03.170
A part of it is quarantined.

09:03.170 --> 09:04.540
Why?

09:04.540 --> 09:06.810
It entered a rest phase

09:06.810 --> 09:10.110
when there was an accident
with an Earth research ship.

09:10.110 --> 09:11.280
Separated?

09:11.280 --> 09:13.250
Where is that portion?

09:15.920 --> 09:17.290
This is, you know...

09:17.290 --> 09:22.360
In the first place, the fact that
I am all alone for this banquet is bad!

09:22.360 --> 09:25.290
As the firstborn
son of the Garsus family

09:25.290 --> 09:28.860
I must go along with
old tradition and invite her.

09:28.860 --> 09:31.700
Old tradition, old tradition...

09:34.570 --> 09:36.560
Old tradition!

09:37.940 --> 09:40.810
You want to see that portion?

09:44.510 --> 09:46.480
We are interacting...

09:46.480 --> 09:50.150
but the other side seems
connected with the Earthlings.

09:50.150 --> 09:52.120
Connected with Earthlings?

09:52.120 --> 09:55.660
The Earthlings' dark,
closed-off feelings of doubt

09:55.660 --> 10:00.390
has turned into a cluster
of the Negative Conscience.

10:00.390 --> 10:04.130
Then that means you're fighting a friend?

10:06.070 --> 10:09.090
You call for each other,
but you're enemies...

10:11.370 --> 10:14.340
You're really lonely yourself, aren't you?

10:20.680 --> 10:24.650
Captain, we will be leaving
the magnetic storm in 5 minutes!

10:24.650 --> 10:26.780
We'll go in one shot!

10:30.290 --> 10:31.360
Finally...

10:31.360 --> 10:32.960
We can go back!

10:32.960 --> 10:35.490
You all did a great job.

10:37.370 --> 10:39.030
Ahem, ahem.

10:40.470 --> 10:41.570
Vice-captain.

10:41.570 --> 10:45.640
Excuse this for being so sudden...

10:45.640 --> 10:49.080
But I have something on my mind...

10:49.080 --> 10:51.810
and put my feelings into a letter.

10:51.810 --> 10:55.580
Please read it as you take
a special pellet to ease fatigue.

10:55.580 --> 10:57.240
Please.

11:01.060 --> 11:03.190
Well... I, if I could...

11:03.190 --> 11:06.630
...for the upcoming
ceremony of the banquet...

11:06.630 --> 11:09.230
...would like to see you alongside me.

11:09.230 --> 11:15.770
That you would a-accept this offer,
I come here.

11:15.770 --> 11:19.870
Now, Vice-captain, your hand.

11:19.870 --> 11:22.470
I'll just accept how you feel.

11:23.540 --> 11:25.050
Just my feelings?

11:25.050 --> 11:27.080
That means...

11:27.080 --> 11:28.740
That means!

11:41.960 --> 11:43.700
We're out of the storm!

11:43.700 --> 11:45.720
We're in the Mejale system!

11:49.870 --> 11:53.010
Then let's start with a toast, everyone.

11:53.010 --> 11:54.810
Cheers!

11:54.810 --> 11:58.450
Don't you all forget
that it's because of me!

11:58.450 --> 12:00.110
You understand?

12:04.550 --> 12:06.320
A place to return to...

12:06.320 --> 12:08.520
Things to protect, huh?

12:08.520 --> 12:11.890
Mr. Alien! Hurry back!

12:11.890 --> 12:13.860
Hurry, hurry!

12:13.860 --> 12:17.020
Geez, quiet down. A-All right.

12:27.410 --> 12:29.380
You were here of all places.

12:29.380 --> 12:31.780
I was looking for you.

12:31.780 --> 12:35.650
Let's go to the others.

12:35.650 --> 12:39.750
The Paksis will feel lonely,
so I'll stay here.

12:42.320 --> 12:44.690
Then I'll stay here as well.

12:49.200 --> 12:50.530
Big Sister.

12:53.500 --> 12:56.240
Hi, I'm back! I'm back!

12:56.240 --> 12:57.770
Welcome back!

12:57.770 --> 12:58.770
Nice work.

12:58.770 --> 13:02.210
Oh, Barnette!

13:02.210 --> 13:05.050
I wanted to see you!
I'm never letting go!

13:05.050 --> 13:08.050
You have to always be with me, okay?

13:08.050 --> 13:10.080
You're overreacting.

13:10.080 --> 13:13.420
It's because you're
so engrossed in Reg...

13:13.420 --> 13:15.950
that you made me lonely!

13:18.160 --> 13:19.490
Jura...

13:23.960 --> 13:26.190
Hey, where's Misty?

13:27.870 --> 13:31.100
Maybe she doesn't fit in here.

13:35.010 --> 13:38.480
I was thinking so
that I wouldn't feel lonely.

13:38.480 --> 13:45.090
Because I would doubt even
the fact that I'm here right now.

13:45.090 --> 13:46.390
But...

13:46.390 --> 13:49.990
right now,
I'm afraid of being all alone.

13:49.990 --> 13:52.690
How ironic.

13:52.690 --> 13:56.030
I used to seek solitude before.

13:56.030 --> 13:59.100
If I didn't trust, I wouldn't be betrayed.

13:59.100 --> 14:02.730
I thought that if I kept my distance,
I wouldn't be hurt.

14:05.510 --> 14:08.070
And I hated myself for thinking that way.

14:09.710 --> 14:12.080
But now it's different.

14:12.080 --> 14:15.480
I would like to stay
myself even if I was reborn.

14:15.480 --> 14:20.550
And I want to be with
everyone that I've met.

14:35.400 --> 14:37.670
Let's go, Misty.

14:37.670 --> 14:39.640
Everyone's waiting over there.

14:42.580 --> 14:46.650
It might be worrisome
to live in a place you don't know

14:46.650 --> 14:50.050
but we're always with you!

14:51.450 --> 14:53.820
You're never alone, Misty!

14:53.820 --> 14:55.820
I know! When we get there

14:55.820 --> 14:58.490
you don't mind rooming with me, right?

14:58.490 --> 15:01.090
There are tons of
toys I want to show you!

15:02.360 --> 15:03.500
You know...

15:03.500 --> 15:07.020
Sorry, but I don't intend
on becoming some UFO fanatic.

15:16.380 --> 15:19.010
It's unusual for a man of Tarak

15:19.010 --> 15:21.920
to be disappointed by a female.

15:21.920 --> 15:24.540
But I'm really sad about this!

15:31.790 --> 15:32.930
It's a minefield!

15:32.930 --> 15:35.230
There are mines set across a vast region!

15:35.230 --> 15:39.000
The floating mines seem
to be Tarak's final line of defense!

15:39.000 --> 15:40.500
For Tarak?

15:40.500 --> 15:42.570
It's an audio signal.

15:42.570 --> 15:46.640
This is the self-defense
system for Tarak space.

15:46.640 --> 15:49.640
Declare your ship's identification code.

15:49.640 --> 15:52.950
If there is no declaration,
we will commence attack.

15:52.950 --> 15:53.950
What now?

15:53.950 --> 15:55.680
I can go out anytime!

15:55.680 --> 15:58.420
No, don't lay one finger on them!

15:58.420 --> 16:01.890
This will stop those coming from Earth,
at least a little.

16:01.890 --> 16:04.410
We can't rush through here!

16:05.560 --> 16:08.860
The defense system has activated!

16:08.860 --> 16:11.430
No declaration of ID code.

16:11.430 --> 16:12.900
Classified enemy.

16:12.900 --> 16:16.300
Now entering defensive attack mode.

16:16.300 --> 16:17.670
Oh, no...

16:17.670 --> 16:20.010
An ID code from Tarak...

16:20.010 --> 16:22.240
Don't you guys have any?

16:22.240 --> 16:25.080
ID codes are for high ranking officers...

16:25.080 --> 16:28.780
For officers in training...

16:28.780 --> 16:31.790
Unfortunately, I don't have one, either.

16:31.790 --> 16:34.380
Damn, neither do I.

16:38.130 --> 16:41.360
The defense system
has targeted the Nirvana!

16:41.360 --> 16:43.760
The countdown has begun!

16:43.760 --> 16:45.830
Targeted and shot by Tarak...

16:45.830 --> 16:47.070
This can't be...

16:47.070 --> 16:49.070
We can't fight Tarak!

16:49.070 --> 16:50.730
We just can't!

16:52.110 --> 16:54.240
We finally made it back...

16:54.240 --> 16:57.210
I thought I finally could go home...

17:00.510 --> 17:02.450
Don't worry.

17:02.450 --> 17:04.510
We'll get home.

17:09.790 --> 17:11.530
The countdown can't be stopped!

17:11.530 --> 17:14.360
120 seconds until they start attacking!

17:19.070 --> 17:21.400
The minefield is getting even closer!

17:21.400 --> 17:25.970
All right, I'll see if I can
destroy the defense system from here!

17:25.970 --> 17:28.080
Wait.

17:28.080 --> 17:29.410
I'll go with you.

17:29.410 --> 17:32.380
You did protect me earlier.

17:35.020 --> 17:36.580
60 seconds left!

17:36.580 --> 17:40.850
Man, if I had known,
I would've asked Grandpa for his!

17:49.460 --> 17:51.990
Less than 30 seconds until attack!

17:54.870 --> 17:59.710
It's more important to release
the target lock than destroy them.

17:59.710 --> 18:01.210
Strange...

18:01.210 --> 18:05.050
I feel less unsure with you.

18:05.050 --> 18:07.910
I like that about you.

18:09.920 --> 18:10.980
10...

18:10.980 --> 18:12.020
9...

18:12.020 --> 18:13.150
8...

18:13.150 --> 18:14.190
7...

18:14.190 --> 18:15.160
6...

18:15.160 --> 18:16.160
5...

18:16.160 --> 18:17.160
4...

18:17.160 --> 18:18.130
3...

18:18.130 --> 18:19.660
2...

18:19.660 --> 18:24.260
Tarak Empire Special Information Bureau:
Tenmei Uragasumi.

18:24.260 --> 18:26.570
Rank: Commander.

18:26.570 --> 18:31.410
ID code: Kanoe-2038.

18:31.410 --> 18:33.270
Begin confirmation.

18:36.640 --> 18:38.250
Confirmation complete.

18:38.250 --> 18:40.650
We look forward to
your ship's noble success.

18:47.990 --> 18:51.020
Ezra, leave a marker at this point.

18:51.020 --> 18:53.030
R-Right!

18:53.030 --> 18:56.330
We will now confine a spy to the brig.

18:56.330 --> 18:58.900
Two security members, come with me.

18:58.900 --> 19:01.500
Who are you?

19:01.500 --> 19:04.070
I'm sorry about this.

19:04.070 --> 19:06.540
There was no other way.

19:09.240 --> 19:11.300
You had known?

19:16.020 --> 19:21.690
Though I have deceived you
for many days, one truth remains.

19:21.690 --> 19:25.460
You are a truly marvelous person.

19:25.460 --> 19:27.390
I am proud of the fact that

19:27.390 --> 19:31.020
though it was a short while,
I was able to serve under you.

19:41.580 --> 19:43.110
Impossible...

19:43.110 --> 19:45.240
She was a he?

20:08.400 --> 20:11.170
What's wrong? Put up the shield quickly.

20:11.170 --> 20:12.140
But...

20:12.140 --> 20:13.800
Hurry.

20:17.040 --> 20:18.280
Don't worry.

20:18.280 --> 20:21.250
Now I won't be able to escape.

20:21.250 --> 20:22.910
Why?

20:24.890 --> 20:26.250
Why?

20:26.250 --> 20:30.390
Why'd the higher-ups
on Tarak go this far?

20:30.390 --> 20:33.230
The situation was
just that bad between us.

20:33.230 --> 20:34.390
But still!

20:34.390 --> 20:36.200
However...

20:36.200 --> 20:42.500
If you had not been a man,
would we have our lives now?

20:42.500 --> 20:43.970
On this ship...

20:43.970 --> 20:48.340
I learned that the education
I received wasn't everything.

20:48.340 --> 20:52.780
I learned that people can change,
depending on their own will.

20:52.780 --> 20:55.250
The truth is aboard this ship.

20:55.250 --> 20:57.270
Right, Vice-captain?

21:00.420 --> 21:04.320
Did I do the right
thing by asking him out?

21:04.320 --> 21:06.130
Or...

21:06.130 --> 21:07.260
Captain!

21:07.260 --> 21:11.200
We're surrounded by Tarak fleets!

21:11.200 --> 21:13.570
No, not just Tarak!

21:13.570 --> 21:16.800
The fleets from Mejale, too!

21:16.800 --> 21:19.000
What the hell? What's this mean?
